<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ductĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		duco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that may be led</i>, <i>guided</i>, or <i>conducted</i> (post-Aug. and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scena,</span>”
				<i>movable</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. G. 3, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flumen aquae riguae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a canal</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 31, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aes,</span>”
				i. e. <i>that may be hammered out thin</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8, 20, § 94 sq.</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Num. 8, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
